; The project's glossary. It holds the policy on names, the terminology
; registry (the Write/Not table that `make lint-terms` holds every other file
; to), and the terms the game or the project coined whose names do not say what
; they are (DEF-6). A term gets an entry only once a code label carries it, and
; terms go in alphabetical order after the two entries below.

[Page:Glossary]
SectionPrefix=Term

[Term:policy-on-names:Policy on names]
A thing takes the name the game gives it. The screen text comes first, then the
instruction leaflet.

A thing the player knows by its picture takes the name of that picture. The code
decides what the thing does.

A name says what a thing is. Its description says what it does, as the code
shows it.

The project names each part of the code before it documents that part in full.
Such a first name can change once the project writes the full description.

The project writes each word as the game spells it, such as defence.

This page defines a word only when the game or the project made it up. The word
alone must also fail to say what it is. Each such word is the word of a label in
the listing.

[Term:one-word-per-thing:One word per thing]
Each word on the left is the one word the project uses for its thing. The words
on the right never name that thing, in a label, a title or a sentence.

#TABLE(default)
{ =h Write | =h Not }
{ control panel | status bar, status panel, scoreboard, dashboard, HUD }
{ Damage Report Indicator | damage meter, damage bar, health bar, energy bar }
{ defence device | defense device, defense, boss }
{ flip, flipped | barrel roll, inverted flight, upside-down mode }
{ hatchway | hatch-way, trapdoor, trap door, airlock }
{ mothership | mother ship, mother-ship, liner, liners, starship }
{ pulse laser | laser cannon, laser gun, blaster }
{ sector | hull-sector }
{ shield | energy shield }
{ Skimmer | craft, spaceship, spacecraft }
{ structure | obstacle, obstacles }
TABLE#
